<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nueva Planta decrees</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1707">1707</a>–<a href="/years/1716">1716</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nueva Planta decrees were a series of laws issued by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-v-of-spain">Philip V of Spain</a> between 1707 and 1716, during and after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>. Punishing the territories of the Crown of Aragon that had backed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> claimant, they abolished the separate laws, parliaments and institutions of Aragon, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a> and Catalonia and imposed the government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, creating a more unified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nueva-planta-decrees.jpg" alt="Nueva Planta decrees" width="320" height="461" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ordenada pel Rei d'Espanya Felip V. Impresa per Joseph Teixidó. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nova_planta_Catalunya_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After the Battle of Almansa, Philip V abolished the laws of Aragon and Valencia by the <b>Nueva Planta decrees</b> of 1707, though Aragonese civil law was partly restored in 1711.</blockquote><a href="/empire/crown-of-aragon">Crown of Aragon · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Because Aragon, Valencia and Catalonia had largely backed the Habsburg claimant, Philip abolished their separate institutions by the <b>Nueva Planta decrees</b> of 1707–1716 and imposed Castilian law and administration.</blockquote><a href="/empire/crown-of-castile">Crown of Castile · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>…claimant Archduke Charles against the Bourbon Philip V. After the Bourbon victory at the Battle of Almansa on 25 April 1707, Philip V abolished the fueros of Aragon and Valencia by right of conquest in a decree of 29 June 1707, the first of the <b>Nueva Planta decrees</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-aragon">Kingdom of Aragon · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>These institutions survived until the <b>Nueva Planta</b> decree of 1716.</blockquote><a href="/empire/principality-of-catalonia">Principality of Catalonia · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>The War of the Spanish Succession confirmed him as king but cost Spain its European possessions at Utrecht in 1713, while the <b>Nueva Planta decrees</b> abolished the separate institutions of the Crown of Aragon.</blockquote><a href="/state/bourbon-spain">Bourbon Spain</a></li><li><blockquote>Majorca remained a separate realm within the Crown until the <b>Nueva Planta</b> decree of 1715.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-majorca">Kingdom of Majorca</a></li></ul></section>
